WEBVTT

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.200
Morning, Shinobu.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.450
Good morning.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.340
<i>It's been a few weeks since I arrived in Japan.</i>

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.460
<i>I've got pretty used to living here.</i>

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.390
<i>Japan is a very easy place to live in.</i>

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.300
That's hilarious!

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.310
Anyway, then she...

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.020
<i>There are lots of foreigners.</i>

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.690
<i>Everyone around me is so nice.</i>

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.870
Alice, it's not summer.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.780
Don't water the plants.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.030
I love Japan.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.820
<i>Oomiya Shinobu.</i>

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.720
<i>Shinobu is ladylike and kind.</i>

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.640
<i>She's the very image of Japanese womanly virtue.</i>

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.400
What beautiful white skin you have.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.190
Isami, good morning.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.360
Good morning.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.020
Onee-chan, do you have work today?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.450
Yeah, in the afternoon.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.910
<i>Isami's a model.</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.040
<i>The two of them are sisters, but they're nothing alike.</i>

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.500
<i>Sort of like these two!</i>

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.420
See you later.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.480
Hooray!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.550
Good morning.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.260
Good morning, Shinobu-chan, Alice-chan.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.770
Hello.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.610
You're so shy.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.320
<i>Speaking to adults still makes me a little nervous.</i>

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.440
<i>So does that dog!</i>

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.820
Alice, you have to greet him first.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.400
I'm scared.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.540
Good morning, Aya-chan.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.500
Good morning, Aya.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.540
Mornin'.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.480
Where's Youko-chan?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.960
She's on duty, so she went on ahead.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.460
Sorry for making you wait.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.960
We should hurry, or we'll be late.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.090
<i>Komichi Aya.</i>

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.470
<i>Aya is intelligent and reliable.</i>

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.850
<i>But sometimes...</i>

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.690
Aya-chan, you forgot to put tights on!

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:08.350
What?!

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.270
Y-You can wear my socks...

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.230
But then, you'll have bare feet!

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.320
Hm, I'm sure I...

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.110
There they are!

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.040
<i>She's a scatterbrain.</i>

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.240
Good morning.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.280
Inokuma Youko.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.250
<i>Youko is cheerful and energetic.</i>

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.460
Mornin'.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.710
Good morning.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.090
You didn't eat breakfast before coming to school this morning?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:39.750
What?

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.110
Yeah, I did...

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.260
Don't act like you don't know what I'm talking about!

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.890
<i>It's good to eat lots of food.</i>

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:52.880
Stand.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.270
Bow.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.680
Good morning.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.110
<i>Alice Cartelet.</i>

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:03.100
<i>I plan to enjoy my Japanese high school life to the fullest again today!</i>

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.460
Alice, how old will you be on your birthday this year?

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.540
What?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.500
I'm a first year in high school, just like you guys.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.170
We're in the same class, aren't we?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.340
Oh, right.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.220
But you're rather short for your age.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.640
I'm 155 cm tall, so...

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.780
...that'd make you around 50 cm.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.060
I'm not that short.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.390
Are you sensitive about your height?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.520
Yeah.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.370
Why?

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.020
Small girls are cute.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.060
That's right.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.360
Don't worry.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.690
You'll grow taller.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:45.570
But I've only grown about three
centimetres since elementary school...

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.160
Well, in that case...

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:48.780
Yes...

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.740
Maybe you won't...

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.350
No!

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.760
Don't say that!

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.210
Is that really so depressing?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.470
Youko...

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.800
What?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.510
Will your chest be small because you're short?

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.310
Yeah.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.100
Your height has nothing to do with that.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:16.960
Yeah.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.400
That's one thing you don't need to worry about.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.650
There's a perfect example right here.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.200
Well, I'm sorry for being flat-chested!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.050
I'm kidding!

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.450
It was only a joke!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.160
Come on, class is starting.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.330
All right.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.330
First period is English.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.620
Shinobu, you like English?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.040
She likes Karasu-chan.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.170
Karasu?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.570
Karasuma-sensei.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:42.500
Our homeroom teacher.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.000
Oh, the lady with the glasses.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.550
That's the one.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.890
She's kind, beautiful, fluent in English, mature, wears tracksuits...

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:51.930
I want to be like her when I grow up.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.680
You like her <i>tracksuits</i>?!

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.690
And that's how you do it.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.190
I feel so nervous having a native speaker in the class.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.900
How's my English?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.290
Your English is the best in Japan, Sensei.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.270
Why, thank you.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.160
<i>A-A rival!</i>

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:18.490
Yes!

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.040
Alice-san.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.210
She spoke in English!

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.700
Amazing!

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:30.050
Impressive, Alice-san.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.930
Everyone, Alice-san will show you how to speak properly.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.130
What?

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.640
Let's start at the top of page 40.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.930
O-Okay.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.850
<i>How did this happen?</i>

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.860
That was amazing when you raised your hand, Alice.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.360
Proper English is something else, isn't it?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.210
Sensei was so happy.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.910
Shino, do you have your textbook?

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.160
Yes.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.030
Shino, where's your pencil case?

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.250
Shino...

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.910
I'm sorry.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.610
What's "Shino"?

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.980
It's a nickname.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.130
It's a name friends call each other.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.570
Friends...

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.010
Oh, it's Sensei!

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:15.970
<i>That's it.</i>

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:20.230
All their faces layer together...

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.230
I will call Shinobu "Shino"!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.610
You must be good friends.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.570
I'm so happy.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.160
<i>Why are they reacting like this?</i>

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.210
Alice, you're so moe!

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.050
What does "moe" mean?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.670
It means you're so cute, you're on fire!

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.180
Wrong kanji, you idiot.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:57.680
What?

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:58.970
That doesn't look right.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.930
The longer I stare at them, the more confused I get.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.020
This character was applied as a phonetic symbol.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:07.940
Really?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:08.790
Yes.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:12.590
It originally comes from a "whoosh" sound effect.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.450
You're teaching them obvious lies again...

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:21.750
Actually, it originally comes from the noise you make when you see something cute.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.210
I see.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.420
That sound effect evolved into the word "moe".

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.040
Who came up with that?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.050
I did.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.910
Sorry I'm late.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:47.110
You're late!

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.480
Only by ten minutes.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.240
Only?

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.270
What do you mean, only?!

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:53.990
I've been here for an hour!

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.280
You're way too serious...

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.410
Shino and Alice still aren't here yet.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.710
I know.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:09:59.870
I'm kind of worried.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.120
What if they got into an accident on the way?

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.700
<i>Why does she treat them so differently?</i>

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.040
I'm sorry we're late.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.420
They're here.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.420
What the heck is that?!

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.760
Shino, are those your clothes?

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:14.850
Yes.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.130
How do I look?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.590
Shino's dressed up as someone.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.220
Ah, so it's a cosplay, is it?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.930
Um, are you a maid?

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.180
A gothic lolita?

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.470
Wrong.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.940
The correct answer is: A foreigner!

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.350
Over-generalisation!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.780
All right.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:10.520
Hm?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:12.810
There's a foreign couple over there.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.480
Are they travelling?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.280
They seem to be having trouble.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.610
I'll go check it out.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.360
What?

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.700
Wait, Shino!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.890
Hello.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.200
Alice!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:27.860
What?

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.230
O-Okay.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.920
Why did she even bother going over?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.760
Shino's interest in foreigners has crossed into the realm of obsessive lately.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:44.720
She liked them enough to do a homestay, after all.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.180
Maybe she'll learn to speak English properly someday.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.560
Wait, an English newspaper?!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.520
But her face says she's not understanding any of it!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.740
Shino, do you like Europe?

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.620
Europe? I like England and France...

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.990
So, Europe, right?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:06.910
What?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.990
Europe... England...

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.110
I'm getting all mixed up.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:13.710
I'll try to draw it.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.840
We live on the planet Earth.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.420
You're starting there?!

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:23.300
Sensei, goodbye.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.680
Goodbye.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.800
I'm thinking of dyeing my hair when I graduate.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:39.620
Really?

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:40.440
What colour?

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.070
Blonde.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.910
I don't know if blonde would work...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.830
Well, not blonde, but a very blondish brown.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:55.920
<i>That's no different.</i>

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.040
It might actually look good on you, though.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.920
<i>Aya, don't tell me you really believe that!</i>

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.340
Shino, you're going to dye your hair blonde?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.720
Yes, then we'll match.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.220
It won't look good on you!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:07.980
Blunt!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:08.640
So like her!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.690
Blonde hair would look strange, wouldn't it?

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.030
Shino, I'm sorry.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.020
I didn't mean to...

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.600
If I dyed my hair blonde,

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.400
it could look so awful, I'd have to be blurred out.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:24.850
Huh?

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:26.620
What are you talking about?

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.530
Now, now.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.580
How you'd look is a matter of opinion.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.660
That's right.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.540
Shino, that outfit you wore yesterday looked really good on you.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.540
<i>What?</i>

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.210
<i>Really?</i>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.580
It did?

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.250
Yes.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:42.300
No one else would have looked as adorable in it as you did.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.880
Thank you.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:47.840
I think blonde hair would really go with that outfit, so I...

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.680
No blonde hair!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.610
Alice, your blonde hair is so beautiful.

00:13:58.610 --> 00:13:59.690
Thank you.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:03.690
But mine is even more beautiful.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.320
No!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:08.560
What's wrong, Alice?

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.870
Did you have a bad dream?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.530
Why don't you look at Shino's face to calm you down?

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.670
Be sure to turn in your career plans by tomorrow.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.340
Sensei, can I ask a question?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.630
What is it, Oomiya-san?

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:31.220
Why did you decide to become a teacher?

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:35.180
Well, let's see... I had become one before I even knew it.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.770
<i>That's not very helpful.</i>

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:41.110
But nothing's more fun than being a student.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:47.200
The toughest thing about being a
student is trying not to get too sleepy.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.150
<i>She looks sleepy now...</i>

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.520
Sensei, look this way!

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.240
Okay.

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:57.890
I've never thought about what I want to do in the future.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.000
Don't worry about it too much.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.590
Just think about what kind of person you want to become.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.590
<i>Shino's amazing.</i>

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.970
I don't have a clear plan,

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.180
but I'd like to become someone who helps others.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.410
I see.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.600
Can I see that?

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.170
What?

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:17.580
S-Sure.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.560
In other words, you want to be this.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:24.980
You left out the important part!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.610
Are you done?

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.860
Well...

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:35.490
I guess I'd like to become an idol and perform at the Budokan!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.250
Just kidding.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.370
That's amazing!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.230
I'm sure you can make that happen, Youko.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.080
I'm behind you all the way!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:42.920
What?

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.750
I was kidding.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.670
It was just a Japanese joke.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.420
Shino, are you done?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.920
Yes, all finished.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:50.800
That was quick.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.720
I've known what I want to be since I was little.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.220
What did you write?

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:56.930
An interpreter.

00:15:57.270 --> 00:15:59.060
Oh, for aliens?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.600
For foreigners!

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.060
Alice has been teaching me English lately.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.070
Really?

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.730
Try translating Alice's English, then.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.940
Very well.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:19.620
Um, "I"... "Japan"... uh...

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.540
Please don't continue before I've finished translating!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.750
What?!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.760
Next time, I'll say it one word at a time.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:30.950
Did you say strawberries?

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.340
I like to eat strawberries plain!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.280
She's got a long way to go.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.960
Aya, you seem like the type of person who'd write "Bride".

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.690
I-I'd never put that!

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:43.070
You're erasing something...

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:45.130
Of course I'm erasing!

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:46.310
It's an eraser!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.190
It's a tool for erasing mistakes!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:49.960
Oh, come on!

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.950
What am I supposed to write, then?!

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:52.950
She's getting defiant!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.080
I wouldn't have any trouble writing my ideal marriage proposal.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.220
Uh-oh.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:00.580
She's in full-on maiden mode now.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:05.580
I think it's best to say it directly, like a man.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.600
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.790
<i> I don't know how to respond...</i>

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.800
For example...

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:12.980
"Be my wife."

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:13.720
Like that?

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.470
Stop it, you stupid-head!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.970
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.230
Alice is deep in thought.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.480
I wonder if she's worried about her future.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:30.980
No, she's looking in the direction of...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.110
England?

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.950
Is she homesick?

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.950
<i>I'm so sleepy.</i>

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.200
She's so small, but she's living in a foreign country all by herself.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.660
Of course she'd get homesick.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.880
We have to protect her.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.970
I'll get it!

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.050
"The beginning... of spring..."

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:01.470
That's too difficult for Alice!

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.350
Allow me to answer!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.690
Alice, where are you going?

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.150
We'll go with you.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.950
I'm just going to the faculty office!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.250
Sensei, my journal...

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:26.990
Alice-san, you came at the perfect time.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.960
Do you like cats or rabbits better?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:32.520
What?

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.630
R-Rabbits?

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.150
I knew it.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.630
It's gotta be rabbits!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.890
<i>What is this?</i>

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.390
Yes, perfect.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.480
Your handwriting is beautiful, Alice-san.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.270
T-Thank you.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.410
I'm glad you've got used to Japanese schools.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.620
You seem to have made lots of friends.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.580
Friends?

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.500
Yes.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.830
<i>Alice, how old will you be on your birthday this year?</i>

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.920
<i>That was amazing when you raised your hand, Alice.</i>

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.380
<i>That's too difficult for Alice!</i>

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.380
Am I wrong?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.270
I wonder what they think of me.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.390
I vote for hamster.

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:28.560
What?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.440
Not rabbit?

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.810
Oh, you're back.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.570
We were talking about going somewhere on the way home.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.610
We're all going to the pet shop again...

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.530
Shino!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:40.030
Yes?

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.540
Answer me honestly!

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.830
What do you think of me, Shino?

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.710
What do I think of you?

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.290
<i>Is she confessing her love for me?</i>

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.280
I don't know what to say to such a sudden confession.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.850
But you're a very important friend to me.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:01.470
Really?

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.300
Yes.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:07.890
More than rabbits or hamsters?

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:10.100
Of course.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.610
Good.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.120
That's great.

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.110
What is?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.070
Does this mean she's not homesick anymore?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:26.330
Alice, why did you come to study abroad in Japan?

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.950
Because I wanted to go to school with Shino, of course!

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.040
Is that really enough of a reason?

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:35.340
She must really love you, Shino.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.210
I've missed you too, Alice.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:51.700
I was thinking about going back to England when I'm older.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:55.610
But since you came to see me, my wish came true.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.360
It's a vapour trail.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.500
I wonder if that plane's heading for England.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.630
It's probably going to Tokyo, judging by its direction.

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:16.550
What?

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:17.500
C'mon, read the mood here!

00:22:55.730 --> 00:22:57.850
I'll hand back your quizzes now.

00:22:58.230 --> 00:22:59.420
Alice-san.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:00.300
Yes.

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:04.850
Very impressive, Alice-san.

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:05.650
You got a perfect score.

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:08.030
Look at this.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:11.620
I gave you a flower.

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.410
It's even got a flag.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:17.080
<i>Homeroom teacher, Miss Karasuma.</i>

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:20.000
<i>She always treats me like a child.</i>

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:23.090
Alice, do you have any interest in dyeing your hair?

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.350
There are so many colours.

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:25.350
It sounds like fun!

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:28.920
I hear black hair is pretty popular among foreigners.

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:29.880
Aya-chan!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.720
Stop... Please stop...

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.370
She's actually crying!

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:35.010
See you next time.
